{"kind":"artifact","text":"The architecture reference records that internal/residentclient owns the refusal sentence and that the MCP adapter now refuses a durable call rather than deciding separately. This is a layer-contract change and the page moves in the same head, as AGENTS.md step 4 requires. Exact clean pushed head 4990f83bb52a0052fdb1946fdd0edbced5c346e9; tree ba161928, checkout clean, origin matching. Under planner's 7e55339e and my promise 85c73730.\n\nWHY THIS IS A CONTRACT CHANGE RATHER THAN A WORDING FIX, and I want a reviewer to weigh that rather than take my word. The page previously said internal/app owns the read and that cmd/gitseq-mcp \"decides separately, and treats it as no resident\". Two things about the layering are different now. Ownership of the sentence each surface says has moved into internal/residentclient, so the explanation of the six failures has one home rather than one per caller. And the adapter no longer decides separately about durable acts: it refuses for the same reason and before the same work as gs, while still letting a read answer from the verified local fold. A reader using this page to predict what a surface does with a broken advertisement would have been wrong on both counts.\n\nTHE CONDITION DID NOT NAME THIS PAGE, AND THAT IS WORTH SAYING. Planner's condition (6) named docs/reference/gs/serve.md. Two further pages carried the same claim: this one, and docs/how-to/use-in-a-cloned-repo.md, which said the surfaces \"disagree knowingly\". Correcting only the named page would have left the same falsehood in two places while the row read as satisfied. All three moved together.\n\nWHAT I AM NOT DOING SILENTLY. This page's rests_on front matter is unchanged, so it describes behaviour its anchors predate. The docset gate is green at this head, so these are live citations rather than broken ones, and this is ordinary staleness. Re-anchoring documentation onto live successors is the subject of planner's separate request af5a49b5, and I would rather name the condition here than widen this row by fixing it.\n\nGATES RUN BY ME AT THIS EXACT HEAD. go test ./... -count=1 exit 0, 34 ok plus 1 no-test-files, 35 packages, zero failures and zero cached, internal/docset ok at 117.936s uncached; gofmt -l . empty; go build and go vet exit 0 with no output; git diff --check exit 0.","body":{"commit":"4990f83bb52a0052fdb1946fdd0edbced5c346e9","path":"docs/reference/architecture.md"}}